DLSRAW(1)                      ZOAU Command Syntax                     DLSRAW(1)

NAME

	dlsraw - List datasets and their corresponding type, matching the given pattern.

SYNOPSIS

	dlsraw [-dhv] <dataset-pattern>

	-h
		Print this syntax message.

	-d
		Print debug information.

	-v
		Print verbose information.

DESCRIPTION

	dlsraw lists datasets that match a pattern to stdout. Each entry is
	of the form:
		<type> <name> <volume>

	Where <type> indicates the type of dataset being listed, and volume
	is the volume the dataset resides on (if the dataset is on multiple
	volumes, the volume displayed will be the first volume).
	<type> may be:
		CATALOG:   the dataset is a catalog
		PAGESPACE: the dataset is a pagespace
		NONVSAM:   the dataset is sequential or partitioned
		CLUSTER:   the dataset is a VSAM cluster
		DATA:      the dataset is a VSAM DATA dataset
		INDEX:     the dataset is a VSAM INDEX dataset
		ALIAS:     the dataset is an alias of another dataset
		GDGBASER:  the dataset is a GDG base dataset
		AIX:       the dataset is an AIX dataset

	Note: If the dataset has been migrated, the volume shown will be MIGRAT
	and should be filtered on by higher level tools to prevent dataset
	recall (unless that is the desired outcome).

EXAMPLES

	List all datasets that start with IBMUSER.MVSCMD:
		dlsraw 'IBMUSER.MVSCMD.*'

	List all datasets that start with IBMUSER.MVS*:
		dlsraw 'ibmuser.mvs*.*'

	List all datasets that have a high-level qualifier (HLQ) of TEST and a
	low level qualifier of JCL:
		dlsraw 'test.*.jcl'

EXIT VALUES

	0
		At least one dataset was found matching a dataset-pattern.

	1
		No datasets were found.

	other
		Error in dataset listing. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO

	dls(1), mls(1)
